  "body": "### Summary\nAs a reader, I want the page items at the end of the top \"…\" menu, after Rechercher and Hors ligne, as #583 and legacy have them, so that the menu reads like the legacy one.\n\nRefs #583 (found in its Mac check; build `cb3da9ce` = `origin/dev-swift`, which contains #583 and #590).\n\n### Observed\niPhone 18 Pro (iOS 27.0, portrait and landscape) and iPad Pro 13\" (iOS 27.0, landscape, regular width), logged in, a 511-page topic. The top \"…\" menu lists, top to bottom, in light, dark, Increase Contrast, XL and AX3 alike:\n\n1. Filtrer les posts\n2. (separator) Première page, Aller à la page…, Page 509, Page 510, Dernière page, Dernier post\n3. (separator) Enregistrer cette page hors ligne, Rechercher dans le sujet\n\n### Expected\n#583's own check list: \"Rechercher, Hors ligne, Filtrer, then the page items\", a separator before the page items. Legacy (`MessagesView.swift:4692-4725` @ 2440d79): Sondage, Rechercher, a divider, then `pageChoiceMenuItems()`. So the page items close the menu.\n\n### Likely cause\nThe overflow is built from four `.secondaryAction` items: Filtrer and the page group are in `TopicReaderView`'s `.toolbar`, while Rechercher (`ReaderSearchFlow`) and Hors ligne (`ReaderOfflineSave`) are added by modifiers applied before that `.toolbar`. The system orders them in its own way, so declaration order inside one `.toolbar` is not enough. Not verified in code beyond this reading.\n\n### Acceptance\n- Top \"…\" order on iPhone and iPad: Rechercher, Hors ligne, Filtrer, separator, page items (or the order the operator picks, written in LOT-186).\n- A test or a Mac check pins the order.\n",
